      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cqbd9zyeb3xnvso",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1120,
      "y": 706,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "text": "(c)  74HC08 unpowered or removed, or a\nbroken TTL cable. (a) and (b) are both on\nthe translator side and do not reach past\nthe AND gate — nothing else covers this.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ldrv",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 1560,
      "y": 560,
      "width": 220,
      "height": 76,
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "label": {
        "text": "Laser driver\nTTL-switch pin"
      },
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cqbd9bl9bivgtepo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1560,
      "y": 646,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "text": "Confirm this input is\nACTIVE HIGH before\nconnecting it. On an\nactive-LOW input every\npull-down above becomes\na FIRE command.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "wz",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 790,
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 150,
      "backgroundColor": "#ebfbee",
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cqbd97xiq2ieyw78",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 58,
      "y": 802,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "text": "WHY THE ONE-SHOT EXISTS",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cqbd95m35ghiqcqs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 58,
      "y": 828,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "text": "Every SOFTWARE mechanism that can end a pulse — enforce_max_pulse, execute_cycle, Laser::fire's re-entry check, the\nwatchdog, the E-stop poll — runs on the control thread. If that thread hangs with GPIO 18 HIGH, none of them fires.\nThe one-shot is not on that thread and needs neither software nor an operator: it is the ONLY autonomous enforcer of the\nduration bound. A normal short pulse passes through unchanged because the AND gate follows GPIO 18; a stuck-HIGH GPIO 18\nis force-cut when Q times out.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "vz",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 1070,
      "y": 790,
      "width": 720,
      "height": 150,
      "backgroundColor": "#fff5f5",
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cqbd9emetd4sx4j8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1088,
      "y": 802,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "text": "MANDATORY SCOPE TESTS — before either laser is connected",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cqbd9d0lhs81jfbi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1088,
      "y": 828,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "text": "1.  10 ms GPIO 18 pulse → equally short laser TTL. If it stretches to the\n    full period, Q is driving the TTL alone: the AND gate is missing.\n2.  GPIO 18 held HIGH → TTL goes LOW at the measured period, stays LOW.\n3.  Pull AHCT125 #2 → TTL stays LOW.  (proves (b))\n4.  Pull SN74HC08N → TTL at the connector stays LOW.  (proves (c))\n5.  Disconnect the GPIO 18 wire → TTL stays LOW.  (proves (a))\n6.  Record the measured period.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cqbd9yfzh30y8ev",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 966,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "text": "Nominal period for a vendor coefficient of 0.45 and the reported 220 kΩ × 1 µF is ≈ 99 ms — but the on-hand device's manufacturer and the passive tolerances are not recorded,\nso THE BOUND IS THE MEASURED ASSEMBLED PERIOD, not the calculation. R/C tolerance alone can swing it ±20 %. At ≈99 ms the hardware sits just below the ~105 ms real\nsoftware bound, so it becomes the binding limit and will also clip legitimate maximum-length pulses. If the backstop should only trip on a failure, raise it above the software\nbound (e.g. C_ext = 1.5 µF → ~130–150 ms) and re-measure.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7cqbd92svseriiug3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 1058,
      "strokeColor": "#e8590c",
      "text": "Residual risk: the '123 is itself a single component, and a broken AND gate or a failed one-shot must be considered in the FMEA. The arm switch and E-stop remain the outer\nlayers and are not on the control thread — but both need a human hand. The monostable is the only autonomous enforcer of the duration bound.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:09:21.937Z",
      "version": 1
    }
  ],
  "appState": {
    "viewBackgroundColor": "#ffffff",
    "gridSize": null
  }
}